#: npc/jobs/2-2/crusader.txt#160 (mes)
- "[Murnak Mijoul]"
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/crusader.txt#161 (mes)
- "Don't linger around in a place like this and forge your own path towards discovering your own strengths. The day that we will join hands in battle will come soon."
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/crusader.txt#162 (mes)
- "A Novice...?"
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/crusader.txt#163 (mes)
- "So green, and yet,"
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/crusader.txt#164 (mes)
- "so much potential."
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/crusader.txt#165 (mes)
- "[Murnak Mijoul]"
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/crusader.txt#166 (mes)
- "Let me assure you that I'm no criminal. I'm here merely to train myself. Perhaps as you become stronger, you will understand."
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/crusader.txt#167 (mes)
- "Hm. You have no business in a place like this. Please leave, and do not interrupt my training."
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/crusader.txt#168 (mes)
- "What do you want...?"
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/crusader.txt#169 (mes)
- "If you have no business here,"
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/crusader.txt#170 (mes)
- "then please leave. A tranquil state of mind is essential in self training..."
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/crusader.txt#171 (mes)
- "[Murnak Mijoul]"
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/crusader.txt#172 (mes)
- "I wish to improve the sense of serenity in my heart in preparation for the Holy War that is to come. So please, do not disturb me."
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/crusader.txt#173 (mes)
- "What is it...?"
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/crusader.txt#174 (mes)
- "Do you have business"
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/crusader.txt#175 (mes)
- "with me, man of the sword?"
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/crusader.txt#176 (mes)
- "with me, woman of the sword?"
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/crusader.txt#177 (select)
- "I'd like to take the Crusader test.:Nothing."
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/crusader.txt#178 (mes)
- "[Murnak Mijoul]"
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/crusader.txt#179 (mes)
- "You wish to become a Crusader...? Hm, fighting in the Holy War is an admirable goal we may both share."
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/crusader.txt#180 (mes)
- "[Murnak Mijoul]"
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/crusader.txt#181 (mes)
- "Your name is"
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/crusader.txt#183 (mes)
- "...?"
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/crusader.txt#184 (mes)
- "Let me take"
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/crusader.txt#185 (mes)
- "a look at your face."
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/crusader.txt#186 (mes)
- "[Murnak Mijoul]"
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/crusader.txt#187 (mes)
- "Hmm. You wish to become a Crusader, but do not wear a Rosary? I have no business with you if you cannot uphold our customs."
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/crusader.txt#188 (mes)
- "[Murnak Mijoul]"
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/crusader.txt#189 (mes)
- "Hmm..."
+ "Hmm..."
#: npc/jobs/2-2/crusader.txt#190 (mes)
- "You seem so-so, but also young and ambitious. Ambition may work against you if it is not tempered with patience."
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/crusader.txt#191 (mes)
- "[Murnak Mijoul]"
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/crusader.txt#192 (mes)
- "Don't give me a reason to doubt you, and show me your patience. You must endure my test with your patience if you wish to become a Crusader."
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/crusader.txt#193 (mes)
- "[Murnak Mijoul]"
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/crusader.txt#194 (mes)
- "You may take my test right away. It's actually quite simple. All you must do is walk to the end of the corridor."
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/crusader.txt#195 (mes)
- "[Murnak Mijoul]"
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/crusader.txt#196 (mes)
- "But..."
+ "Mas..."
#: npc/jobs/2-2/crusader.txt#197 (mes)
- "You must keep one thing in mind. Under no condition are you allowed to kill the monsters."
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/crusader.txt#198 (mes)
- "[Murnak Mijoul]"
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/crusader.txt#199 (mes)
- "Well then..."
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/crusader.txt#200 (mes)
- "Good luck."
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/crusader.txt#202 (mes)
- "[Murnak Mijoul]"
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/crusader.txt#203 (mes)
- "You seem to have a lot of time on your hands. Why don't you do something more productive, like pick Jellopy off the streets or something?"
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/crusader.txt#204 (mes)
- "What is it...?"
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/crusader.txt#205 (mes)
- "You're the Swordman from before. What happened, did you fail?"
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/crusader.txt#206 (select)
- "Let me retake the test.:What kind of test was that?!"
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/crusader.txt#207 (mes)
- "[Murnak Mijoul]"
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/crusader.txt#208 (mes)
- "I'll let you retake the test as much as you like. But if you continuously fail, there's an inherent problem with your"
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/crusader.txt#209 (mes)
- "state of mind."
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/crusader.txt#210 (mes)
- "[Murnak Mijoul]"
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/crusader.txt#211 (mes)
- "Wait..."
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/crusader.txt#212 (mes)
- "Where have you left your Rosary? You can't let that lie around just anywhere. We are supposed to be warriors of holiness."
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/crusader.txt#213 (mes)
- "[Murnak Mijoul]"
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/crusader.txt#214 (mes)
- "Carelessly losing things is an attitude for mere Swordsmen. If you really want to retake the test, you must respect the Crusader traditions."
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/crusader.txt#215 (mes)
- "[Murnak Mijoul]"
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/crusader.txt#216 (mes)
- "Your problem is your habit of hitting monsters the moment you see one. You must develop your patience and endurance."
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/crusader.txt#217 (mes)
- "[Murnak Mijoul]"
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/crusader.txt#218 (mes)
- "Just focus..."
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/crusader.txt#219 (mes)
- "Your only goal is to walk from one end of the corridor to the other. It's simple when you think"
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/crusader.txt#220 (mes)
- "about it."
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/crusader.txt#221 (mes)
- "[Murnak Mijoul]"
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/crusader.txt#222 (mes)
- "No matter what you do, do not kill any of the monsters. This time, think carefully before you draw your sword."
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/crusader.txt#223 (mes)
- "[Murnak Mijoul]"
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/crusader.txt#224 (mes)
- "Well then..."
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/crusader.txt#225 (mes)
- "Good luck."
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/crusader.txt#227 (mes)
- "[Murnak Mijoul]"
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/crusader.txt#228 (mes)
- "Who are you to say that you don't like my test? With that kind of attitude, you'll never become a Crusader."
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/crusader.txt#229 (mes)
- "[Murnak Mijoul]"
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/crusader.txt#230 (mes)
- "I can understand if you are easily frustrated, but you must overcome your frustration to pass this test."
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/crusader.txt#231 (mes)
- "Hmm, seems like you did well. It shouldn't have been too hard. You no longer have any business"
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/crusader.txt#232 (mes)
- "with me."
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/crusader.txt#233 (mes)
- "[Murnak Mijoul]"
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/crusader.txt#234 (mes)
- "For your next test, go look for Gabriel Valentine in the Prontera Sanctuary. Well then, I'll see you around."
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/crusader.txt#235 (mes)
- "Hmmm..."
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/crusader.txt#236 (mes)
- "You still have tests to complete if you want to become a Crusader, don't you?"
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/crusader.txt#237 (mes)
- "[Gabriel Valentine]"
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/crusader.txt#238 (mes)
- "Welcome, fellow Crusader."
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/crusader.txt#239 (mes)
- "How is your training"
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/crusader.txt#240 (mes)
- "coming along?"
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/crusader.txt#241 (mes)
- "[Gabriel Valentine]"
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/crusader.txt#242 (mes)
- "You must not forget to train everyday, and prepare for the day the Holy War will come upon us."
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/crusader.txt#243 (mes)
- "Welcome, I am a Crusader."
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/crusader.txt#244 (mes)
- "I am preparing for the"
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/crusader.txt#245 (mes)
- "foretold Holy War"
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/crusader.txt#246 (mes)
- "that is to come."
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/crusader.txt#247 (mes)
- "[Gabriel Valentine]"
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/crusader.txt#248 (mes)
- "If you are interested in becoming a Crusader, you must train first as a Swordman. Come and visit us again when you believe that you have learned enough as a Swordman..."
