#: npc/jobs/2-2/monk.txt#2 (mes)
- "[Tohobu]"
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/monk.txt#3 (mes)
- "Hmm? What business do you have here?"
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/monk.txt#4 (mes)
- "If you wish to enter this sacred area,"
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/monk.txt#5 (mes)
- "you must give me your name and job level!"
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/monk.txt#6 (mes)
- "[Tohobu]"
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/monk.txt#7 (mes)
- "....Eh?"
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/monk.txt#8 (mes)
- "Oh!^FF0000gosh^000000! I am sorry, I think I misunderstood you from someone I know."
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/monk.txt#9 (mes)
- "[Tohobu]"
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/monk.txt#10 (mes)
- "......."
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/monk.txt#11 (mes)
- "........"
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/monk.txt#12 (mes)
- "[Tohobu]"
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/monk.txt#13 (mes)
- "It is odd...I never misunderstand people...oh, well. Have a good day."
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/monk.txt#14 (mes)
- "[Tohobu]"
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/monk.txt#15 (mes)
- "Hmm? What business do you have here?"
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/monk.txt#16 (mes)
- "If you wish to enter this sacred area,"
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/monk.txt#17 (mes)
- "you must give me your name and job level!"
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/monk.txt#18 (mes)
- "[Tohobu]"
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/monk.txt#19 (mes)
- "Now, please tell me your name and job level."
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/monk.txt#20 (select)
- "Ignore him.:Tell him."
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/monk.txt#21 (mes)
- "[Tohobu]"
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/monk.txt#22 (mes)
- "To ignore another is disrespectful, get out!"
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/monk.txt#24 (mes)
- "[Tohobu]"
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/monk.txt#25 (mes)
- "Hmm... "
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/monk.txt#26 (mes)
- " is your name?"
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/monk.txt#27 (mes)
- "...did I say it right?"
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/monk.txt#28 (mes)
- "Okay, and your job level is "
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/monk.txt#29 (mes)
- " correct?"
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/monk.txt#30 (mes)
- "[Tohobu]"
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/monk.txt#31 (mes)
- "Very well... why have you come here"
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/monk.txt#33 (mes)
- "?"
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/monk.txt#34 (select)
- "To visit and learn about monks.:I wish to become a monk...:I'm tired and need to rest..."
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/monk.txt#35 (mes)
- "[Tohobu]"
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/monk.txt#36 (mes)
- "I see..."
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/monk.txt#37 (mes)
- "We monks live our lives for spiritual enlightenment."
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/monk.txt#38 (mes)
- "We improve our bodies as well as our minds to reach true inner peace."
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/monk.txt#39 (mes)
- "May you find your inner peace as well."
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/monk.txt#40 (mes)
- "[Tohobu]"
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/monk.txt#41 (mes)
- "Hmm you seem as though you have been training for this..."
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/monk.txt#42 (mes)
- "That is good. Go see our sensei Moohae. Speak with him."
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/monk.txt#43 (mes)
- "He will help you start your training."
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/monk.txt#44 (mes)
- "[Tohobu]"
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/monk.txt#45 (mes)
- "Hmm, you do not seem ready to become a monk."
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/monk.txt#46 (mes)
- "To become a monk you must be,"
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/monk.txt#47 (mes)
- "at least a job level 40 Acolyte."
+ ""
#: npc/jobs/2-2/monk.txt#48 (mes)
- "If not, you are not yet ready to become a monk."
+ ""
